<div class="tale-introduction"><p class="eyebrow">THE GODDESS AS PROTECTOR</p><p>This original English retelling follows <strong>Devi Mahatmya, chapters 2–4</strong>, within the Markandeya Purana. It includes the manifestation of the Goddess, the battle with Mahishasura and the hymn that follows. Extended combat, gift lists and prayers are condensed.</p></div>
<section class="story-characters" aria-labelledby="characters-title"><p class="eyebrow">MEET THE CHARACTERS</p><h2 id="characters-title">Characters in this story</h2><dl><div><dt>Devi</dt><dd>The Goddess, addressed here as Chandika and Ambika and honoured as Durga.</dd></div><div><dt>Mahishasura</dt><dd>The buffalo-form asura who has displaced the gods and changes shape in battle.</dd></div><div><dt>The gods</dt><dd>Those who seek refuge, offer their gifts and praise the Goddess.</dd></div><div><dt>The lion</dt><dd>The Goddess’s mount and an active participant in the battle.</dd></div><div><dt>Cikshura and Chamara</dt><dd>Commanders who lead attacks before Mahishasura’s final confrontation.</dd></div></dl></section>
